'''acoustical''' (ạ-kös′- or ạ-kous′ti-kạl), ''a.'' Of or belonging to the science of acoustics; acoustic.
{{smaller block|The acuteness of the blind in drawing conclusions from slender ''acoustical'' premises. {{right|''Science'', VI. 195.}}}}

'''acoustically''' (ạ-kös′- or ạ-kous′ti-kạl-i), ''adv.'' In relation to acoustics or hearing.

'''acoustician''' (a-kös- or a-kous-tish′ạn), ''n.'' One skilled in the science of sound; a student of acoustics.
{{smaller block|The transverse vibrations . . . were the only ones noticed by the earlier ''acousticians.''
